.TH HERROR 3
.SH NAME
herror, hstrerror \- network database interfaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
#include <netdb.h>
.br
#include <arpa/inet.h>
.SH DESCRIPTION
hstrerror returns a static message for HOST_NOT_FOUND, TRY_AGAIN, NO_RECOVERY or NO_DATA. herror writes the optional prefix, message for h_errno and a newline to standard error.
.PP
Database entries and aliases use static storage, overwritten by the next call for that database. These interfaces are not reentrant. Lookup matches canonical names and aliases. set*ent rewinds an open file and keeps it open after lookups when stayopen is nonzero; end*ent closes and clears stayopen.
.PP
Malformed records and physical lines of 1024 bytes or more are skipped. A record supports 35 aliases. Comments begin with #. Lookups return NULL on missing entries or I/O failure.
